# cite-citadel workspace configuration — auto-loaded from the workspace root (no python-dotenv).
# This top section is all most setups need. Everything below the "Advanced" line is optional
# tuning: the defaults are right for most workspaces, and `citadel doctor` flags misconfiguration.
#
# No API key needed: ingest shells out to a coding-agent CLI you are already logged in to, under
# your own account and your provider's terms — see the README "License & third-party tools"
# section. Full per-knob reference: docs/configuration.md.

# Which CLI ingest shells out to, run AGENTICALLY (autonomous file tools): claude | copilot | agy.
# (agy = Google's Antigravity CLI, the successor to the retired gemini CLI.)
CITADEL_LLM_CLI=claude

# Model for EVERY backend: passed through as --model to claude, copilot and agy alike.
# claude: an alias (sonnet | opus | haiku) or a full id. copilot: e.g. claude-sonnet-4.5 or auto.
# agy: an id from `agy models`. Leave it unset to run the CLI's own default model.
# Whatever actually served the session is what gets stamped per source — this knob is the REQUEST,
# the manifest/`citadel status`/the viewer record the model the backend REPORTED.
# CITADEL_INGEST_MODEL=

# Per-session CLI timeout in seconds; raise it for opus or large raw files.
# CITADEL_LLM_TIMEOUT=1200

# Target language of ALL wiki prose, whatever the sources' languages (verbatim quotes stay original).
# CITADEL_WIKI_LANG=en

# Free-text steer for ingest sessions ("create one machine registry from the maintenance lists").
# Usually passed per run as `citadel ingest --guidance "..."` instead of set here; guidance steers
# WITHIN the rules and never overrides citations. Permanent house rules belong in rules/local.md.
# CITADEL_INGEST_GUIDANCE=

# How many OTHER raw sources one session may consult when its own source uses a term/code/reference
# it never explains (found through the wiki, cited to the file it came from — core.md § Related
# sources). A per-session ceiling, so one ingest never sweeps the raw tree; 0 = never look.
# CITADEL_RELATED_SOURCES=3

# Write one transcript per source (prompt + full CLI output) here; relative = under the workspace root.
# CITADEL_LLM_LOG_DIR=.citadel_llm_logs

# ============================== Advanced (optional) ==============================
# Long-form explanations for every knob below — plus the "Local models (Ollama)" recipes for
# running ingest fully on your own machine or LAN — live in docs/configuration.md.

# --- Paths & multi-root ---
# Relative values resolve against the WORKSPACE ROOT; absolute values may point outside it (e.g. a
# mounted network drive — out-of-workspace sources are keyed by absolute path and fully supported).
# Wiki and raw work best under a common parent or with both roots configured explicitly;
# `citadel doctor` checks that citation links actually resolve ("workspace coherence").
# CITADEL_WIKI_DIR=wiki
# CITADEL_RAW_DIR=raw
# CITADEL_DOCS_DIR=docs
# Multiple raw roots: a comma/newline list, each walked by ingest. When set it REPLACES the walk
# list (include `raw` to keep the workspace root); CITADEL_RAW_DIR stays the primary root.
# CITADEL_RAW_DIRS=raw, /mnt/share/dept-docs

# --- Formats: images, PDF, audio, Office dedup ---
# Read image files visually instead of rejecting them as binary; 0 keeps images out of the wiki.
# CITADEL_IMAGE_SUPPORT=1
# PDF mode: text | images — "images" also reads figures/charts (needs a backend that renders PDFs).
# CITADEL_PDF_MODE=text
# PDF text-layer pre-pass: auto | 1 | 0. pypdf ships as a bundled dependency, so PDFs ingest via
# an extracted, cached text layer (.citadel_pdftext/ next to the wiki) — real `lines A-B` locators,
# offline-verifiable by lint/wiki_raw, and large PDFs chunk correctly. "auto" (default) uses it
# whenever pypdf imports (it does by default); 0 forces agent-native PDF reading (`p. N` locators,
# agent-verified).
# CITADEL_PDF_TEXT=auto
# Transcribe audio/video files (.mp3/.wav/.m4a/.mp4/...) with a LOCAL whisper-class CLI and ingest
# the [HH:MM:SS]-stamped transcript (cached in .citadel_transcripts/ next to the wiki); needs the
# binary below installed. Off by default.
# CITADEL_AUDIO_SUPPORT=0
# The whisper-class binary — a PATH name or absolute path. Must speak the openai-whisper flags
# (`<file> --output_format srt --output_dir <dir>`; whisper-ctranslate2 / mlx_whisper are
# drop-in compatible) — docs/configuration.md "Audio/video sources".
# CITADEL_WHISPER_CLI=whisper
# Optional model passed as `--model` (e.g. turbo | small | large-v3); empty = the CLI's default.
# CITADEL_WHISPER_MODEL=
# Per-file transcription timeout in seconds (CPU transcription of a long recording is slow).
# CITADEL_WHISPER_TIMEOUT=3600
# Same-folder document exports sharing a basename (report.pptx + report.pdf): ingest only ONE
# (PDF first, then modern Office, then legacy); 0 ingests every format separately.
# CITADEL_DEDUP_BY_BASENAME=1

# --- Throughput ---
# How many sources ingest folds in CONCURRENTLY (`citadel ingest --jobs N` overrides per run).
# 1 = the serial default. Higher runs that many agent sessions at once, each on its own staging
# copy; promotes stay serialized and a source that raced another over the same page is re-run
# serially. Trade-off: concurrent sessions cannot see each other's new pages, so cross-linking
# suffers — see docs/configuration.md "Parallel ingest".
# CITADEL_JOBS=1
# Circuit breaker: stop the run after this many CONSECUTIVE sources come back from the agent
# having changed NOTHING (0 disables it). Catches an agent CLI that runs and exits 0 but cannot
# actually do its work — a self-update mid-run, a revoked permission — before it bills a session
# for every remaining source. Only sources expected to change something count; a reconcile's
# "nothing changed" is a real verdict and never counts.
# CITADEL_STALL_LIMIT=3

# --- Large sources & repos ---
# A source longer than this many chars is folded in over several merging passes; 0 disables chunking.
# CITADEL_MAX_SOURCE_CHARS=300000
# Resume checkpoints for those chunked sources: a run that dies at segment N continues there next
# time instead of re-paying for segments 1..N-1 (the wiki still only ever gets fully-imported
# sources). 0 = off; the banked segments live in .citadel_resume/ beside the wiki.
# CITADEL_RESUME=1
# A raw/ sub-folder that is a git checkout (or carries a .citadelsource marker) is ingested as ONE
# size-capped digest tracked by its HEAD commit; 0 falls back to the per-file walk.
# CITADEL_REPO_SUPPORT=1
# Repo digest tuning: total character budget, and the per-file cap inside it.
# CITADEL_REPO_DIGEST_MAX_CHARS=120000
# CITADEL_REPO_PER_FILE_MAX_CHARS=8000

# --- Wiki history (git) ---
# Commit the wiki dir after every run that changed it: auto = only when wiki/ is already its own
# git repo, 1 = also `git init` it on first use, 0 = never. Best-effort — never fails a run.
# CITADEL_WIKI_GIT=auto
# Optional push target after each commit — a remote name (origin) or URL; empty = commit locally only.
# CITADEL_WIKI_GIT_REMOTE=git@github.com:you/my-wiki.git

# --- Curate ---
# Model for `citadel curate` sessions (often cheaper than ingest); unset reuses CITADEL_INGEST_MODEL.
# CITADEL_CURATE_MODEL=haiku
# Free-text STRUCTURAL steer for curate sessions ("retitle the machine pages to '<no> <model>'"):
# naming, routing, splits, merges, cross-links — never a fact, its wording, or its citation.
# Usually passed per run as `citadel curate --guidance "..." <paths>`, where the named pages are
# curated even if no detector flagged them.
# CITADEL_CURATE_GUIDANCE=

# --- Hermetic sessions ---
# Keep your PERSONAL agent configuration (~/.claude hooks, CLAUDE.md context, MCP servers) out of
# ingest sessions by passing the CLI's isolation flag (claude --bare). Only passed when the
# installed binary advertises the flag, so older CLIs run unchanged; 0 deliberately runs sessions
# with your personal config. copilot/agy have no such flag today.
# CITADEL_HERMETIC=1

# --- Serving (MCP) ---
# In-memory page cache for `citadel serve`: the server holds the last wiki load and re-checks it
# with a stat-only walk on every call, instead of re-parsing the whole wiki per MCP tool call.
# auto (default) = on in `citadel serve` only, 1 = on wherever citadel reads the wiki, 0 = never.
# Nothing is persisted, and ingest/curate always read from disk.
# CITADEL_PAGE_CACHE=auto

# Remote serving: `citadel serve --http` speaks MCP's Streamable HTTP transport so a client that is
# NOT on this machine (claude.ai, a phone via a tunnel) can reach the wiki. It refuses to start
# without a token, and every request must send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
# Generate one: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# CITADEL_HTTP_TOKEN=
# Bind address/port/path. Loopback default: this transport is PLAIN HTTP, so reach it through a
# tunnel that terminates TLS (cloudflared, tailscale, ssh -R) rather than binding 0.0.0.0.
# CITADEL_HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# CITADEL_HTTP_PORT=8765
# CITADEL_HTTP_PATH=/mcp
# When 1, the HTTP server disables the two mutating tools (wiki_capture, wiki_ingest): they stay
# listed, but answer with a refusal, so only the eleven readers act — recommended for anything
# reachable beyond your own machine.
# CITADEL_HTTP_READ_ONLY=0
# Which `Host` headers the server accepts (anti-DNS-rebinding). Unset = derived from the bind
# address, which is right for a direct loopback bind and wrong behind a tunnel or proxy: those
# forward their OWN hostname, so name it here or every request is refused with 421. A 0.0.0.0 bind
# derives nothing and refuses to start until this is set; `*` accepts any Host.
# CITADEL_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=your-tunnel.example.com
# Browser Origins admitted. Unset = none: a request carrying any Origin is refused, which is right
# for non-browser MCP clients. Name one (or `*`) only for a browser-based client.
# CITADEL_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://claude.ai

# --- Observability ---
# Stream each agent session's output live (the claude CLI prints only its final result envelope —
# use CITADEL_LLM_LOG_DIR above for a full claude record). CLI flag: -v.
# CITADEL_LLM_VERBOSE=0

# --- What discovery skips ---
# OS/junk globs skipped at discovery (Thumbs.db, .DS_Store, ~$ locks, swap/backup files, ...).
# A comma/newline list REPLACES the built-in defaults; a `+` prefix ADDS to them.
# CITADEL_IGNORE_PATTERNS=+*.bak,~backup*
# Size ceiling in BYTES: a raw file bigger than this is skipped at discovery — never hashed, never
# ingested — and listed on the run report and in `citadel status`. The size-based complement to the
# name-based patterns above, for a raw root that also holds machine data (a folder of multi-GB
# sensor dumps costs a full sha256 stream per file before anything can call it unreadable binary).
# 0 (the default) = no limit; an explicitly named path (`citadel ingest big.tdms`) always wins.
# CITADEL_MAX_SOURCE_BYTES=52428800

# --- Style profiles ---
# When 1, first-person sources also yield attributed, dated, cited opinions plus a per-person
# writing-style profile; leave off for many-person corpora.
# CITADEL_STYLE_PROFILES=0

# --- Binary overrides ---
# Override a CLI binary's path when it is not on PATH.
# CAUTION in a SHARED workspace (this .env lives on a network drive several machines mount):
# these are absolute, machine-specific paths and apply to EVERY machine — a path under one
# user's home directory breaks the CLI for everyone else. Keep such overrides in each user's
# shell environment instead of this file.
# CLAUDE_CODE_PATH=/home/you/.local/bin/claude
# COPILOT_CLI_PATH=/home/you/.local/bin/copilot
# AGY_CLI_PATH=/home/you/.npm-global/bin/agy
# The model recorded per source is the one the backend REPORTED for that session, so no
# per-backend model env var is consulted — docs/configuration.md "Backend selection".
